  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R8-046$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A task is stuck because two teams each think the other team owns the next step. Both teams meet their own measures while the shared result suffers. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Bring both sides together, clarify the handoff, and agree one owner$qb$, $qb$Contact the other team and ask who can take the next step$qb$, $qb$Escalate the delay to both managers immediately$qb$, $qb$Complete the other team's step yourself without agreement$qb$, $qb$Wait until one team accepts responsibility$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R9-030$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A new teammate completes a task correctly but takes much longer than expected. The aim is to build independent judgement. What is the best coaching response?$qb$, $qb$Ask them to explain their process, then help identify where time can be saved$qb$, $qb$Show them one faster method and let them practice it$qb$, $qb$Tell them they need to work faster next time$qb$, $qb$Take over the task whenever speed matters$qb$, $qb$Compare their speed publicly with an experienced teammate$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R9-031$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague owns a task you delegated and asks you to approve a small decision within the agreed limits. The colleague needs meaningful authority within clear limits. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Remind them that the decision is within their authority and let them decide$qb$, $qb$Confirm that they can decide and ask them to keep you informed$qb$, $qb$Approve it this time so the work keeps moving$qb$, $qb$Take back decisions that could affect the outcome$qb$, $qb$Require approval for all future decisions$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R9-032$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team is busy with several useful activities, but one has little connection to the current goal. Accepting the work would displace an agreed priority. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Reduce or stop the low-value activity and redirect effort to the goal$qb$, $qb$Review whether the activity still has a useful purpose$qb$, $qb$Keep it because the team has already invested time$qb$, $qb$Continue until the next planning cycle$qb$, $qb$Add more people so all activities can continue$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R9-033$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague in another team will be affected by a change you are making tomorrow. The stakeholder needs enough notice to adjust their own plan. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Tell them before the change, explain the effect, and check what they need$qb$, $qb$Send them a short advance notice about the change$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager and assume the message will reach them$qb$, $qb$Inform them after the change is complete$qb$, $qb$Wait until they notice the effect$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
