  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-25PLUS-R03-031$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An executive you empowered makes a controversial decision within agreed boundaries, and several peers ask you to overrule it before results are known. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Protect legitimate delegated authority, test only whether boundaries or material new evidence have changed, and avoid teaching the organization that escalation defeats empowerment.$qb$, $qb$Improve the current model incrementally while retaining its core incentives, assumptions and decision structure.$qb$, $qb$Seek additional stakeholder input but do not establish how contradictory evidence or interests will be resolved.$qb$, $qb$Make a unilateral short-term choice that reduces visible tension but leaves the systemic mechanism unchanged.$qb$, $qb$Avoid intervention because changing an established model could create additional uncertainty.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
