  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-25PLUS-R09-033$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A profitable project could significantly alter a culturally important landscape even though legal approvals are obtainable. What is strongest?$qb$, $qb$Assess cultural and stakeholder value alongside economics and law, engage affected groups meaningfully, explore alternatives and include residual impact in the final decision.$qb$, $qb$Take a credible immediate action on the visible issue and defer broader institutional implications to the next governance cycle.$qb$, $qb$Gather more evidence and make a limited adjustment without resolving the central enterprise trade-off.$qb$, $qb$Preserve the current framework and ask affected leaders to manage the consequences within their areas.$qb$, $qb$Maintain the existing course until external events make change unavoidable.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
